the electrical calculators.\\\"}]]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"article\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-12 px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 text-slate-600\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"1. Current from power\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"table\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"thead\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-slate-950 text-white\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 text-left\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Circuit\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 text-left\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Active power\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"th\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 text-left\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Apparent power\\\"}]]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tbody\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"divide-y divide-slate-200\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 font-bold\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"DC\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"P = V × I\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Not separately modeled\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 font-bold\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Single-phase AC\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"P = V × I × cos φ\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"S = V × I\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3 font-bold\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Balanced three-phase AC\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"P = √3 × V × I × cos φ\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"p-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"S = √3 × V × I\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Three-phase voltage is line-to-line. The tool assumes a balanced load. Unbalanced phase and neutral-current studies are outside this engine.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"2. Conductor resistance versus temperature\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"When no manufacturer resistance is entered, the engine uses R = ρL/A with a linear temperature correction referenced to 20 °C. Reference values are 0.017241 Ω·mm²/m and α = 0.00393/°C for 100% IACS copper, and 0.028265 Ω·mm²/m and α = 0.00403/°C for 61% IACS conductor-grade aluminum. For real cable products, manufacturer resistance data is preferred because strand construction and product details can change actual resistance.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"3. Voltage drop\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6 font-mono text-sm leading-7 text-slate-800\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"DC: ΔU = 2 × I × L × R\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Single-phase AC: ΔU = 2 × I × L × (R cosφ + X sinφ)\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Balanced 3-phase AC: ΔU = √3 × I × L × (R cosφ + X sinφ)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"R and X are per-length cable values and are divided by the number of equal parallel conductors. Cable length is entered as the one-way source-to-load distance. Percentage drop is ΔU ÷ source voltage × 100.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"4. Real cable power loss\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The tool uses conductor resistance, not reactance, for real power dissipation. DC and single-phase two-wire loss is 2 × I² × R × L; balanced three-phase loss is 3 × I² × R × L. Annual energy loss multiplies the operating loss by entered hours/day and 365 days. Annual cost is annual lost kWh × the user-entered energy tariff.\\\"}]]}],\\\"$L12\\\",\\\"$L13\\\",\\\"$L14\\\"]}]]}],null,\\\"$L15\\\"]}]\\nd:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$1\\\",\\\"h\\\",{\\\"children\\\":[null,[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L16\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":\\\"$L17\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"hidden\\\":true,\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L18\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$19\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Next.Metadata\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$L1a\\\"}]}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"meta\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"next-size-adjust\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"\\\"}]]}]\\nf:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"link\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"rel\\\":\\\"stylesheet\\\",\\\"href\\\":\\\"/_next/static/chunks/4179cl1w4j930.css\\\",\\\"precedence\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"crossOrigin\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"nonce\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\"}]\\n1b:I[97367,[\\\"/_next/static/chunks/2pq2d3eit8abw.js\\\"],\\\"OutletBoundary\\\"]\\nc:C\\n10:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-center text-xs text-slate-500 md:text-left\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"© \\\",2026,\\\" Green Engineering Tools. All rights reserved.\\\"]}]\\n11:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"max-w-2xl text-center text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500 md:text-right\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Engineering decision-support tools. Formal compliance, certification and site-specific electrical design remain subject to applicable standards, manufacturer data and qualified professional review.\\\"}]\\n12:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"5. Wire-size recommendation boundary\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-4 leading-7\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The automatic wire-size result searches the standard AWG/kcmil or metric catalog for the smallest size that meets the chosen voltage-drop target at the design current. It does not invent a worldwide ampacity table. Thermal ampacity depends on jurisdiction, cable insulation, installation method, grouping, ambient temperature, terminations and other corrections. If you already know the allowable ampacity of the selected cable after those checks, you can enter it manually in advanced inputs and the calculator will compare it with design current.\\\"}]]}]\\n13:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"6. Reference sources\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ul\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-5 space-y-4 text-sm leading-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/hb/nbshandbook100.pdf\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-black text-emerald-700 hover:underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"NIST / National Bureau of Standards — Copper Wire Tables\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"br\\\",null,{}],\\\"Reference copper temperature coefficient and conductor-resistance background.\\\"]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/circ/nbscircular346.pdf\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_